ty are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Closed vocabularies by exhaustive enumeration against an independent oracle written from pinned SPEC v0.7.0 \\\\u00a713.14.2 (10548+): the seven dispositions, the five profiles, the strategies, and every closed core reason code are admitted exactly; every other token (case variants, whitespace, near-misses, empty, non-string) is refused with a literal code; a reverse-DNS extension reason is admitted but can never redefine or shadow a core code; each has a narrowing its named test kills when run alone\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"FidelityDispositionRecord rules pinned over the full (disposition x reason-set-cardinality x canonical_object_id presence x source-evidence presence) grid: exact requires an empty reason set, every other disposition at least one reason, synthesized requires no source canonical object, every non-synthesized row traces to captured source evidence; field bounds (string lengths, sorted-unique arrays) refused at edge and edge+1\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Fidelity Report 1.0.0 closed schema: exact member set, fidelity_report_id as the JCS digest with only that member omitted (independently recomputed in the test), archive vs target branch-exact nullability, dispositions sorted unique by source item key with synthesized rows after source rows, counts/event_kind_counts/content_block_counts/byte_counts/reason_counts derived from the rows and reconciled exactly; a report whose aggregates disagree with its rows is refused\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate x entry census with the domain axes above in the conformance matrix and TRACEABILITY, isolated kill attribution, importer outcome grid keyed (package, entry, input) with moved classes named; task_delta scope (no registry edit; the Story final leaf carries it)\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ship\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4001,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1001,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
