{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c715","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d002-d967-7243-a1ef-6e798194c920"},"sequence":485,"recorded_at":1780531400000965,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f82f9d2-9d92-4e29-bde0-42d341e3fcad","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f82f9d2-9d92-4e29-bde0-42d341e3fcad","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f82f9d2-9d92-4e29-bde0-42d341e3fcad"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d004-cf62-7750-9849-5ff08a9cfa44"},"task_id":"01a0d004-cf62-7750-9849-5ff08a9cfa44","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d004-cf62-7750-9849-5ff08a9cfa44","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-2ya5le/boardpull2/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2ya5le/TASK-260830-2ya5le_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2ya5le Results — implement-fidelity-report-and-reason-registry (rev3 rework)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-21bxa3`, tip `0ca3e4c`);\n5|no commit on the Story branch. This is the FIRST leaf of\n6|STORY-260830-21bxa3; the Change Request is `task_delta` (no\n7|registry edit — the Story's final leaf carries it).\n8|\n9|Rev3 answers review verdict rev2 (`unmeasured-build-utf8-sites`,\n10|CHANGES REQUESTED) per `TASK-260830-2ya5le_rework-rev3.md`: close\n11|the CLASS, not the three sites. The invariant is that every\n12|string-valued member of every shape this leaf builds or decodes\n13|refuses invalid UTF-8 at every entry with `ErrInvalid` and a\n14|pinned literal detail. The `byte_counts` stated bound is kept\n15|exactly as the orchestrator accepted it; the reviewer held every\n16|other row, and nothing unrelated was rewritten.\n17|\n18|Rev3 delta vs the rev2 candidate tree `7bade702`, measured by\n19|`cmp` per file (`rev2-tree-compare.log` in the evidence tar): all\n20|10 production files byte-identical, all 9 existing test files\n21|byte-identical; only `testdata/mutant_harness.py` differs (8 new\n22|rows + the trailing-newline fix) and\n23|`internal/clonefidelity/utf8_reflection_test.go` is new, plus\n24|TRACEABILITY wording. Zero production bytes changed, as the\n25|rework brief requires.\n26|\n27|Authority: the task record's v0.5.0 §13.14.2/§13.14.4 is STALE per\n28|the brief. All behavior is pinned to `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n29|§13.14.2 \"Fidelity, projection, and lineage\" (line 10548+), quoted\n30|in code comments and tests.\n31|\n32|## What was built (rev3)\n33|\n34|- `TestUTF8RefusalReflectionGrid`\n35|  (`internal/clonefidelity/utf8_reflection_test.go`): derives the\n36|  33 string-carrying members from `FidelityReportInput` /\n37|  `DispositionRecordInput` by reflection (asserted non-empty; a new\n38|  string field fails the test until probed; a new unhandled kind\n39|  fails loudly in the walker) and drives member × 5\n40|  invalid-UTF-8 classes (lone continuation `80`, `ff fe`,\n41|  overlong `c0 af`, encoded surrogate `ed a0 80`, truncated\n42|  sequence `e2 82`) × both entries = 330 cells. Build cells pin\n43|  member-specific literals; decode cells pin the frame literal\n44|  `fidelity report not valid UTF-8 (frame)`, because the landed\n45|  `environ.DecodeStrictObject` gate trips before any member\n46|  dispatch — member-level decode attribution would re-implement\n47|  the landed frame parser, which the composition rule forbids.\n48|  The per-member plants prove no member's bytes bypass the frame\n49|  gate. Stated plainly in the matrix (§A row 33, §D).\n50|- `TestRegistryPredicatesRefuseInvalidUTF8`: the 5 remaining\n51|  string-taking public entries × 5 classes return false.\n52|- `TestBuildUTF8ExtensionsNestedDepth`: the delegated extension\n53|  UTF-8 gate fires below the top level (nested map, slice) at\n54|  both layers. `TestBuildUTF8` is kept green as committed.\n55|- 8 new narrowing rows `N-build-utf8-*`: the three reviewer sites\n56|  (`source_class`, `target_locator`, `forbid_reasons`) plus one\n57|  per shape and the remaining explicit pre-marshal sites\n58|  (`source_item_key`, `explanation`, the reason-codes arm, both\n59|  extension call sites). Each admits exactly the `ff fe` token\n60|  and is KILLED by the grid run alone. The reason-codes kill\n61|  arrives via the downstream vocabulary literal (documented in\n62|  the row note). The decode side carries no plant: invalid bytes\n63|  trip the shared strict frame first, which `N-frame-report` /\n64|  `N-frame-row` already pin.\n65|- `mutant_harness.py` trailing blank line removed\n66|  (`git diff --check` clean; untracked files additionally\n67|  scanned).\n68|\n69|Explicit bounds (named, not waived): tuple-sub-member UTF-8\n70|enumeration belongs to `sessadapter` (this leaf pins per-tuple\n71|refusal × 5 classes at both tuple members and both entries);\n72|decode-side attribution is frame-level by landed-owner design\n73|(driven per member, not waived). Both are in the matrix §D.\n74|\n75|## AC coverage: 39 of 40 rows driven + 1 stated bound (measured)\n76|\n77|`TASK-260830-2ya5le_conformance-matrix.md` (attached, §E now\n78|complete — the rev2 attachment was truncated mid-table): 40 AC\n79|rows, 39 driven through a production entry by a named committed\n80|test; every gate row carries a directly-reddening narrowing (§A).\n81|The rev2 reviewer measured 38 fully driven + row 33 partial (4 of\n82|7 sites) + 1 bound; rev3 drives row 33 over the full 33-member\n83|derived class, so the measured ratio is back to 39 of 40 + 1\n84|stated bound (row 24, byte-aggregate reconciliation; owner: spec\n85|clarification (agent-session-manager-spec) + the §13.14.1\n86|capture-manifest leaf). Rows 34–36 are admitted properties /\n87|cross-checks with no gate to narrow (disclosed, not waived).\n88|Nothing here claims `byte_counts` is row-reconciled.\n89|\n90|## Mutants\n91|\n92|`internal/clonefidelity/testdata/mutant_harness.py`: 70 narrowing\n93|rows + harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Battery executed\n94|TWICE on the final tree, exit 0, 71/71 `ok:` lines each run (70\n95|KILLED + control SURVIVED), one raw log per plant per run\n96|(`mutants/run1/`, `mutants/run2/` in the archive, 71 logs each).\n97|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` (verified:\n98|no such files under the package after the runs).\n99|\n100|## Validation rerun (rev3 run, final tree, all exit 0)\n101|\n102|All 30 configured commands from `task-board.config.json`\n103|(`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`), exits observed\n104|firsthand (logs `cmds/cmd*.log`; race as `race/race-G1…G4.log` +\n105|`race/race-sessquery.log`; every log carries its command line +\n106|output + exit):\n107|\n108|- 1 gofmt check: 0. 2 build: 0. 3 vet: 0.\n109|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v`: 0 — 45 packages `ok`, 2865\n110|  top-level PASS (rev1 2862 + 3 new tests), zero FAIL.\n111|- 5 race gate: 0 in 5 bounded groups with `-timeout 25m`\n112|  (44/44 `ok` in G1–G4 + sessquery `ok` 532.4s; zero `DATA\n113|  RACE`). Grouping is process-identical to `./...` (one process\n114|  per package either way). One rerun was needed: the first G1–G4\n115|  attempt passed bare `internal/...` paths (setup failure, my\n116|  invocation error, no product signal); the corrected `./…`\n117|  rerun is the logged evidence.\n118|- 6 cover gate: 0 — 45 `ok`; `clonefidelity` 97.5%,\n119|  `clonebundle` 86.7%, `environ` 92.4% of statements.\n120|- 7–23 fuzz gates (rpcwire ×4, scalar ×1, canonicaljson ×4,\n121|  secconftest ×8, each `-fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`): all 0.\n122|- 24 tracecheck: 0 (`clauses_discharged=70/574` — registry\n123|  untouched). 25 cataloggen `-check`: 0.\n124|- 26 linux build: 0. 27 windows build: 0. 28 JSON sweep: 0.\n125|- 29 `task-board validate`: 0. 30 `git diff --check`: 0.\n126|- Brief extras: `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`: 0;\n127|  importer set (clonefidelity/clonebundle/environ/sessadapter/\n128|  scalar/canonicaljson): all `ok`; new UTF-8 tests `-count=3`:\n129|  0; clonefidelity `-v` 699 pass lines / 0 FAIL; whitespace scan\n130|  of the new/edited untracked files: 0 issues.\n131|\n132|## Handoff state\n133|\n134|Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff\n135|snapshot (4 modified landed files + new `internal/clonefidelity/`;\n136|scratch-index tree `9870fb42e454a1163b4fc6abd778210260cf84d9`\n137|over base `0ca3e4c`). Checklist: all items verified true this\n138|run — checked. Attached (rev3): `TASK-260830-2ya5le_results.md`\n139|(this file), `TASK-260830-2ya5le_conformance-matrix.md`,\n140|`TASK-260830-2ya5le_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (real gzip, under\n141|1 MiB: rev3 gate logs + 142 per-plant logs + `MANIFEST.sha256`).","final_result":true}}}
